We give the proof in detail for the sake of self-containedness. Let us first show the first statement. The Duhamel formula implies  egin{align} \<e^{-itH}\psi,\varphi\>=\<e^{-itH_0}\psi,\varphi\>-i\int_0^t\<V_2e^{-irH}\psi,V_1e^{-i(r-t)H_0}\varphi\>dr,\quad \psi,\varphi\in L^2. \end{align} Plugging $\varphi=G(t)$, integrating over $t\in [-T,T]$ and using Fubini's theorem, we learn by the formula \eqref{adjoint_1} of the adjoint $\Gamma_{H_0}^*$ that $$ \<\<e^{-itH}\psi,G\>\>_T=\<\<e^{-itH_0}\psi,G\>\>_T-i\<\<V_2e^{-itH}\psi,V_1\Gamma_{H_0}^*G\>\>_T. $$ Applying \eqref{proposition_abstract_2_1}, \eqref{proposition_abstract_2_3} and \eqref{proposition_abstract_2_6}, we then obtain the first assertion (1). In order to prove the second assertion (2), we replace $t$ by $t-s$ and plug $\psi=F(s),\varphi=G(t)$ and integrate over $s\in [0,t]$ in \eqref{proof_proposition_abstract_2_1} to obtain  egin{align*} \<\Gamma_HF(t),G(t)\> &=\<\Gamma_{H_0}F(t),G(t)\>-i\int_0^t\int_s^t\<V_2e^{-i(	au-s)H}F(s),V_1e^{-i(	au-t)H_0}G(t)\>d	au ds\ &=\<\Gamma_{H_0}F(t),G(t)\>-i\int_0^t\<V_2\Gamma_HF(	au),V_1e^{-i(	au-t)H_0}G(t)\>d	au. \end{align*} As above, integrating in $t\in [-T,T]$ and using \eqref{adjoint_1} implies  egin{align} \<\<\Gamma_HF,G\>\>_T=\<\<\Gamma_{H_0}F,G\>\>_T-i\<\<V_2\Gamma_HF,V_1\Gamma_{H_0}^*G\>\>_T. \end{align} Exchanging the roles of $H$ and $H_0$, we also obtain  egin{align} \<\<\Gamma_HF,G\>\>_T=\<\<\Gamma_{H_0}F,G\>\>_T-i\<\<V_1\Gamma_{H_0}F,V_2\Gamma_{H}^*G\>\>_T \end{align} Now applying \eqref{proposition_abstract_2_2}, \eqref{proposition_abstract_2_3} to \eqref{proof_proposition_abstract_2_2} implies  egin{align} |\<\<\Gamma_HF,G\>\>_T|\le s_2
